# Gosai

## Lore

The Gosai are soft-spoken killers from another planet, brought to the Palladium World as assassins and spies during the Elf-Dwarf War. Once tree-dwellers, those on Palladium have grown tough scaly skin against the Baalgor Wastelands. They are slender, graceful and hairless, covered in fine metallic red scales, with small pointed teeth and light yellow eyes with golden goat''s-eye pupils, and favor loose tunics, billowing leggings and Bedouin robes.

Level-headed and methodical, they become ruthless, merciless fighters once moved to violence, and can hold a vendetta for generations - yet stay calm in combat and hide their passions from all but their closest friends and family. They despise gluttonous materialism: a Gosai owns no more than he can carry, shuns beasts of burden and vehicles, cares little for gold or gems, and lives for reputation, glory and infamy. There are no known Gosai communities on Rifts Earth.

**Alignment:** Any, but usually selfish or Aberrant evil.

**Size:** 5-6 feet (1.5-1.8 m). **Weight:** 150-175 pounds (68-79 kg).

**Average Life Span:** 60 years.

**Habitat:** Gosai cannot stand cold or wet climates; the Baalgor Wastelands and other deserts are the only places they feel comfortable.

## GM Notes

Gosai prefer Men at Arms O.C.C.s, City Rats of any kind, and wilderness and roguish occupations. Their enemies are Giants, Trolls, Ogres and Orcs, and above all the Quorians, whom they fought throughout the Elf-Dwarf War; on Rifts Earth they take an instant dislike to the Xiticix, Brodkil and demonkind. Their allies are humans, Elves and the Eandroth - on Rifts Earth any reptilian D-Bee, the Lyn-Srial included - and they are indifferent to most others. On Rifts Earth plastics and ceramics give them safe substitutes for metal.
